Nothing third-party is vendored or shipped yet. When Desk is built, these ship or are linked:

CWSDPMI
  A DOS protected-mode extender, Copyright (C) 1995-2010 Charles W Sandmann. Its binary
  distribution may be redistributed unmodified, with CWSDPMI.DOC, under the terms in that file.
  It ships beside the Desk as a separate program.

JEMMEX
  An EMS memory manager (the Jemm project), for programs that need expanded memory. It ships
  beside the Desk as a separate program under its own licence, which will be recorded here with
  its provenance when it is added.

DJGPP (linked into the Desk's executables)
  The cross-compiler and its C library and runtime come from https://www.delorie.com/djgpp/ and
  are provided by the build image or fetched into vendor/, which is not committed.

DOSBox Staging (used to run tests headless; not distributed here)
  GPL-2.0-or-later. https://www.dosbox-staging.org

The design reference in design/ was produced in a design-agent brainstorm. It is not built or
shipped, and its bundled design-system files (design/_ds) are Liminal HQ's own.
